# User Project & Antigravity Craftsmanship Boundaries

Apply this rule whenever a Paperclip agent, harness, or adapter interacts with external user projects (such as `D:\Sanatan_Watch` or other repositories).

## 1. Project Sovereignty
- External user projects are governed exclusively by the user's `autonomous-skills.md` and Pragmatic Engineering guidelines.
- Never modify protected core directories (`src/`, `android/`, build scripts) unless explicitly requested and approved by the human gatekeeper.
- Never apply Paperclip-internal build rules (`rules/*.mdc`) to external user repositories.

## 2. Skill Namespacing
- Paperclip internal operational skills are strictly namespaced under `paperclip-*` (e.g., `paperclip-board`, `paperclip-converting-plans-to-tasks`, `paperclip-create-agent`).
- Domain craftsmanship skills are loaded from `D:\antigravity-skills\` (e.g., `ui-ux-pro-max`, `modern-web-guidance`, `flutter-expert`, `code-review-checklist`).
- Never overwrite or shadow domain craftsmanship skills.

## 3. Tool & Runtime Reuse
- Reuse existing host toolchains (Puppeteer MCP, Git, PowerShell, Capacitor/Flutter CLI).
- Do not install separate duplicate browser binaries, background daemons, or redundant npm packages.
